  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n> unexpected-solidus-in-tag\n> This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+002F (/) code point that is not a part of a **quoted** attribute value and not immediately followed by a U+003E (>) code point in a tag (e.g., <div / id=\"foo\">). In this case the parser behaves as if it encountered ASCII whitespace.\n\nthis section says that a slash is whitespace if it's not part of a *quoted* attribute value, implying that slashes would be replaced in unquoted attribute values, but the section on attribute values suggests that they're allowed and every browser me and a friend have tested allow it. this seems to be a mistake, and should just be \"an attribute value\".",
